atform:windows","name":"platform:windows","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","number":16,"title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5796,"closed_issues":0,"state":"open","created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T09:35:07Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-02-13T20:13:06Z","updated_at":"2026-02-17T20:09:43Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/116259","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116259","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116259.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116259.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"I found when working on my Godot project that crashes could happen. Some I believe might be new instabilities in Godot 4.6 and others are often my own mistakes in a GDExtension. However, if symbols can't be found, the stack looks like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\nDumping the backtrace. Please include this when reporting the bug on: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues\r\n[0] <couldn't map PC to fn name>\r\n[1] <couldn't map PC to fn name>\r\n[2] <couldn't map PC to fn name>\r\n[3] <couldn't map PC to fn name>\r\n[4] <couldn't map PC to fn name>\r\n[5] <couldn't map PC to fn name>\r\n[6] <couldn't map PC to fn name>\r\n```\r\n\r\nAt least showing the module name plus offset is possible when symbols are not available. I believe this could be useful in many cases, especially when crashes happen in other DLLs. To test my changes, I deleted PDBs and put a crash in the editor and ran it. The output is now:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[0] godot.windows.editor.x86_64+0x21a50ce\r\n[1] godot.windows.editor.x86_64+0x21a30fd\r\n[2] godot.windows.editor.x86_64+0x18a14e4\r\n[3] godot.windows.editor.x86_64+0xbe74e\r\n[4] godot.windows.editor.x86_64+0x87fc2\r\n[5] godot.windows.editor.x86_64+0x87de7\r\n[6] godot.windows.editor.x86_64+0x88059\r\n[7] godot.windows.editor.x86_64+0x5aa1016\r\n[8] KERNEL32+0x2e8d7\r\n```\r\n\r\nI also confirmed when PDBs are available they continue to be used as expected.\r\n\r\nNote this exposed a null-termination issue in get_mod_info which was using std::vector<char> to copy strings without the null-terminator. This caused the dbghelp to read past the buffers which sometimes caused the `SymGetModuleInfo64` that I needed to use to give back garbled text. Once I fixed and simplified that, the garbled text was fixed.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116259/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116259/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}